<title>UK: IRA calls ceasefire - Irish state radio.</title>
<headline>IRA calls ceasefire - Irish state radio.</headline>
<dateline>BELFAST 1997-07-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish Republican Army guerrillas plan to call a ceasefire from noon (1100 GMT) on Sunday, Irish state radio RTE said on Saturday.  </p>
<p>RTE said the IRA made its announcement in a message.</p>
<p>It said the guerrillas would declare &quot;an unequivocal restoration of the ceasefire of August, 1994&quot;.</p>
<p>The IRA called a truce in late August ,1994, but broke it in February, 1996.</p>
<p>The statement said that &quot;all IRA units have been instructed accordingly&quot;.</p>
</text>
